## WHAT THE DRAFTER FOUND (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER: a scratch `git clone --no-hardlinks` of the project checkout at `21a07e3c` (equal to BASE for every path read, above), its own `npm ci` against `package-lock.json` sha256 `37e5add354e5...`, Node v24.22.2, jest 29.7.0)
1. **The two routes at BASE.** `GET /api/setup/data-sources` (registration line 17163) reads every active source, and for each enabled one decrypts the stored source (`getDataSourceDecrypted`), builds a client (`createLawClient`) and runs `testConnection()`. `GET /api/debug/data-sources` (line 18393) does the same for every enabled non-primary source and queries 5 rows; its body carries `hasDecryptedSecret`, `workspaceId`, `authMode` and, on success, a `sampleRecord`. Neither handler holds a role check. Measured on the real server (the new cells below, run red-first at BASE): a viewer is answered **200 with 2 connects and 2 stored-source reads** on the setup list (two enabled sources) and **200 with 1 and 1** on the debug read (one non-primary); every non-administrator role of the permission table and the role value `Admin` read the same. This is the ticket's measurement, reproduced.
2. **The edit is the RD-1011 form: three lines at the top of each handler** (two comment lines and `if (!(await requireAdminFor(req, res))) return;`), 6 added lines in `backend/server.js`, none removed; `requireAdminFor(` then appears 40 times (38 at BASE, by `grep -o -F | wc -l`).
3. **The commission's partition is too narrow for the ticket (finding; Q-0 of the report).** The ticket requires "the role inventory and its page are regenerated" and "the suite counts are regenerated by the project's own command", and three older test files pin the old answers. Measured by the drafter's full prototype: with ONLY the commission's paths changed, five cells outside them go red (the red-proof list of `judge2032.py redproof` names them: RD-793 `N2` and `C2`, RD-988 `T7`, RD-978's "review's probe" cell), and the inventory census reads the two rows changed. **Tuesday's default (Q-0): OWNS-B2032 below adds six paths** (`docs/role-capabilities.json`, `docs/ROLE-CAPABILITIES.md` (both written ONLY by the project's own generator), `__tests__/rd793-...`, `__tests__/rd988-...`, `__tests__/rd978-...` (each the narrowest form of the new answer, the way pull request 236 rewrote them), and `scripts/verify-expected-counts.json` (written ONLY by `npm run verify -- --maxWorkers=2 --update-counts`)). `__tests__/rd929-capability-design-census.test.js` (commission-owned) needs NO change: its census cells pass after the move (measured green). PR 236, the sibling change, touched the same file classes (14 paths).
4. **RD-1030's census cell requires the table move.** The cell RD-1030 added (an inventory route that refuses a viewer must not sit under a capability the viewer holds) would turn red if the two rows stayed under `config.read` after the wire changes. So `backend/services/capabilities.js` moves `'GET /api/debug/data-sources'` (line 156) and `'GET /api/setup/data-sources'` (inside line 159) from the `config.read` block (opens line 151) to the end of the `admin.read` block (opens line 175; the RD-1030 rows are line 182), with a two-line comment. RD-1034's two comment edits in that file: line 26 `the 205 routes` becomes `the 203 routes` (the inventory has 203 rows and `ROUTE_CAPABILITY` 203 keys, by `node -e` over both files) and line 96's about text of `admin.read` gains `, and the data-source reads that use stored sign-in details`.
