6. **The cells.** A new file `__tests__/rd1021-setup-list-and-debug-read-administrator-only.test.js` (268 lines, 14016 bytes, 35 tests: 12 `test(` and 3 `test.each(` by the indented pattern, column-1 count 0; 2 `describe(`). It boots the real server twice through the project's harness (`bootServer`) with the inventory's own environment and a preload written at run time that loads the inventory's preload and counts `getDataSourceDecrypted` calls (the ticket's F-3: reads as well as connects). Cells: every non-administrator role of `ROLE_CAPABILITIES` (read at run time: 9 roles) plus the near-miss value `Admin`, on both routes, 403 with `Admin access required`, 0 connects, 0 reads (R1, R2); a viewer's query string, trailing slash and HEAD on both (V1); no session 401 with 0 and 0 (N1); the administrator 200 with at least 1 read and 1 connect on each (A1, A2: the controls); the open window answers an anonymous caller 200 and connects (O1, O2); the first statement of each handler (S1, S2); the table rows under `admin.read` and no non-administrator role holding it (P1); neither route on the pending list (P2); the committed inventory rows (I1, I2); the source-making control (M1).
7. **Red-first, green, red-proof (by `judge2032.py`).** At BASE with only the new file added: **28 failed, 7 passed, 35 total** (exactly the named 28: R1 and R2 for 10 shapes, V1 for 3, S1, S2, P1, I1, I2). In the edited tree: the 25 suites of `suites2032.txt` read **352 of 352 passed** in about 21 seconds. With ONLY the two server.js gates reverted (`apply2032.py <tree> product-revert`): five suites, **29 failed of 81** (the 25 wire and source cells of the new file, RD-793 N2 and C2, RD-988 T7, the RD-978 probe); `roles-foundation-route-census` stayed green in that run (it compares the route SET, which does not move). The full verify: see finding 9.
